**Definition 9.2 (the continuing full mathematical problem).** For the
same exact channel and binary effect at each strength, the unresolved
coherent-input task is to evaluate (CA.28) on every positive complex
$3\times3$ input, including rank-deficient and subnormalized inputs,
and hence to determine all twelve original individual closed minima.
The unresolved full-frontier task is to determine every undominated
original twelve-vector outside, as well as on, the sharp-average face,
with actual common realizations and exact original constraints. A
spectral membership lift, compact parametrization or existence theorem
is not an evaluated formula or such a frontier classification.
Known endpoint laws from RE remain available; the open coherent task is
their general-strength completion, rather than a recomputation of those
endpoint results.

The exact class remains all finite common CP encoders and full TP
decoders in Definition 2.3, with all finitely generated refinements and
arbitrary finite jointly counted quantum fibres. A choice of real,
sign-covariant, JR-conditioned, diagonal, pure-encoder or isometric-decoder
families may provide competitors or proofs of sufficiency, but cannot
replace that universal class in a lower bound. In particular binary-live
freedom below $s=1$ cannot be discarded. No per-history installed map,
input prior or acceptance division is introduced to turn the continuing
problem into a smaller one.

